From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - allow building on ARCH_BCMBCA

The Broadcom BCA SoCs BCM4908, BCM63158, BCM6858, BCM47622 and BCM6756
have an SPU-M crypto engine, fed through a PDC mailbox. The Broadcom SDK
drives it with forks of this driver: an SPU-M only one for BCM47622
(bcmdrivers/opensource/char/spudd/impl4), and a newer one that maps an
SPU-M (brcm,spu_type 1, also the default) to SPU_TYPE_SPUM /
SPU_SUBTYPE_SPUM_NS2 (spudd/impl5). That is what the "brcm,spum-crypto"
compatible of this driver selects.

Nothing in the driver is specific to iProc, so allow it on ARCH_BCMBCA.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
@@ -763,7 +763,7 @@ source "drivers/crypto/virtio/Kconfig"
 
 config CRYPTO_DEV_BCM_SPU
 	tristate "Broadcom symmetric crypto/hash acceleration support"
-	depends on ARCH_BCM_IPROC
+	depends on ARCH_BCM_IPROC || ARCH_BCMBCA
 	depends on MAILBOX
 	default m
 	select CRYPTO_AUTHENC
